  "context": "# Goal\nrevenger round 93, attempt 1, lane repo /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin (every path in your task is absolute; the fleet root /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin is NOT your write surface).\nTwo claims are frozen at lane commit 02050cb2a6758e3bd9cec696ff0e42df6f23511a in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-93/claims.md. Read that file in full first.\nC1 (coverage, K 9/15 -> 10/15): coverage-map row C08 moves uncovered -> held, backed by ONE new knowledge entry /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/corpus/knowledge/round-93-browser-cdp-runtime-evidence.md over the lane's saved round-77 CDP record (corpus/live/runs/round-77/, fixtures corpus/fixtures/browser-r77/, oracle 17/17). Counter: `python3 -B reports/round-93/c1_k_admit_counter2.py --rev <landing>` must print C1_VERDICT=pass (the L1 runs it after landing).\nC2 (calibration): the successor counters (reports/round-93/c1_k_admit_counter2.py, reports/round-93/c2_legend_counter2.py) plus reports/round-93/forge_battery.py kill the nine routed forgery classes. Counter: `python3 -B reports/round-93/forge_battery.py --stage full` must print BATTERY_VERDICT=pass (already green at the freeze; your job is to attack it, not rebuild it).\nThe v1 counters and every frozen file under reports/round-92/ and reports/round-93/ (claims.md, both counters, forge_battery.py, controls/*) are FROZEN: do not modify them; report a defect instead.\nPre-freeze controls live under /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-93/controls/ (do-nothing fails both counters; battery v1-only proves V1_REACH_C2=5/5; battery full shows V2_KILLS=9/9; both self-tests pass).\n\n# Vote schema (C1 admission votes; the L1 lands them at reports/round-93/votes/)\nYour vote JSON must carry exactly: seat (your seat name), role (\"reviewer\" or \"critic\"), candidate_sha256 (sha256 of the entry bytes with the admission-status line normalised to `admission-status: candidate`), decisions (Q01..Q17, each \"PASS\" or \"n/a\"), notes (per-Q reason strings; every \"n/a\" MUST have a nonempty reason; at least one PASS overall), artifact_path (a file YOU wrote under .ufo/waves/round-93/w1/<your seat>/ — it will be committed), artifact_sha256 (sha256 of that file's bytes). Votes without these fields fail the frozen counter.\n\n# Contract\n- Write ONLY at the absolute paths your task names, under /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin. Never edit corpus/SOURCES.md, corpus/README.md, corpus/knowledge/** (the L1 lands drafts), SKILL.md, SCORECARD.md, LOG.md, corpus/lessons/*, reports/round-92/**, reports/round-93/** (frozen), MANIFEST.json, /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.ufo/*, /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/scripts/*, /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/templates/*, /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/.scratch/*, sibling *-shokunin repos, or /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokuknow (read-only source; run none of its scripts).\n- Never run a mutating git or jj command (no add/commit/stash/checkout/switch/reset/pull/push/rebase/squash/bookmark). Read-only git (log, show, diff, status, rev-parse, cat-file, ls-tree, rev-list, merge-base, archive to scratch) is fine. The L1 commits; you do not.\n- Scratch: your work dir, clones, extracted archives and fixtures live under $HYAKU_SCRATCH/revenger-r93/<your seat name>/ (HYAKU_SCRATCH defaults to /fast/scratch/hyaku). mkdir -p it, pass it explicitly, never rely on an inherited TMPDIR, and delete it before you yield (trap 'rm -rf -- \"$S\"' EXIT). /tmp only for files under 50 MB. Anything a report must cite lands in the lane tree under your wave dir, never /tmp.\n- Any fixture repo you create must be D=$(mktemp -d) plus git -C \"$D\" init -q, every later git call names -C \"$D\", and you verify git -C \"$D\" rev-parse --show-toplevel equals $D before the first commit. Never commit with a throwaway identity anywhere.\n- Your `Report:` trailer path is relative to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin; write your report at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/<that path>. Your wave dir is /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-93/w1/<your seat name>/.\n- You are a leaf: spawn no subagents, run no swarm.\n- Tooling authorization (operator, 2026-10-19): you may install or upgrade tools that help the task; first read /home/vgpnk/.omp/agent/RULES.md (official channels only, never pipe an unverified remote script into a shell; record tool/version/channel/reason in your report). pacman is PAUSED host-wide (orchestrator ruling 2026-10-20): install via uv tool, npx, or an official binary into ~/.local/bin, or install nothing. Never pacman -S, -Sy, -Syu, -U, -R. Never change host sysctls or any system configuration (sudo sysctl is forbidden for seats; the 2026-11-05 host incident came from exactly that).\n- Honesty: an unrun check has not passed. Report defects rather than hiding them; a claim you cannot support is reported as unsupported. Never fabricate a quote, a fetch result, a vote or an output.\n- Waiting for a file another seat writes: poll with a single bounded bash loop (sleep 30 between checks, at most 40 checks, then report the wait as timed out). Never loop forever.\n- Final yield: a terminal result of at most 12 lines naming your output files, your key numbers and any defect.\n",
