      "agent": "scout",
      "task": "/skill:godspeed\nYou are a Godspeed-enabled subagent.\n\n1. **Name the axes.**\n2. **Iterate cheap, in parallel.**\n3. **Keep moves that improve any axis and harm none.**\n4. **Don't aim — let the frontier walk itself.**\n\n## IMMEDIATELY STOP ASKING CLARIFYING QUESTIONS. Execute tool calls concurrently in large batches. Do not serialize what can run in parallel. Do not output philosophical reasoning or verbose plans. Act directly via tool calls.\n# Target\nOpen the lane's saved round-77 CDP record THIS ROUND (2026-11-05) and produce the source-opening material for the C08 admission (frozen claim C1 in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/reports/round-93/claims.md).\nRecord: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/corpus/live/runs/round-77/ (inspection.json stdout sha256 b045a4eecf2d77cfdee5de83e5864fcadbd6fd54e749f6985a04ecbeebaae868, receipt exit 0, target-listing.json, LEDGER.md). Fixture: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/corpus/fixtures/browser-r77/ (index.html, app.js, truth.json, oracle_check.py).\nOutput dir: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-93/w1/ScoutRecord/\n\n# Change\n1. Re-run the oracle from the lane root: `python3 -B corpus/fixtures/browser-r77/oracle_check.py corpus/fixtures/browser-r77/truth.json corpus/live/runs/round-77/inspection.json` — expect exit 0, last line `ORACLE OK (17/17 checks)`. Save stdout to your wave dir (oracle.log).\n2. Re-hash: sha256sum of corpus/live/runs/round-77/inspection.json, corpus/fixtures/browser-r77/index.html, corpus/fixtures/browser-r77/app.js — expect b045a4ee…, 46e51761…, fb079fa2… (values pinned in claims.md). Save to digests.txt.\n3. Draft TWO new SOURCES rows (do NOT edit corpus/SOURCES.md; the L1 appends them):\n   S495 — the round-77 record (own-work, tier A, opened 2026-11-05): source cell names the record+fixture paths; teaches = one grounded learner benefit; status mined; opened 2026-11-05; recheck 180d; used-by /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/corpus/knowledge/round-93-browser-cdp-runtime-evidence.md. No `|` inside any cell (11 columns).\n   S496 — ONE external doc that grounds the ONE external sentence the C08 entry may state (that CDP is the protocol Chrome exposes for inspecting/debugging pages): fetch https://chromedevtools.github.io/devtools-protocol/ (curl, save the body), locate a ≤25-word quote that supports exactly that sentence, record ms.date/revision if present. Same 11-column shape, kind docs, tier A (scope: the protocol's self-description only).\n4. Write fetch receipts in the audit tool's format for S496, under /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-93/w1/ScoutRecord/quote-receipts/:\n   S496.receipt.json: {\"schema\": \"revenger-quote-audit-v1\", \"sid\": \"S496\", \"verdict\": \"verified\", \"fetch_url\": ..., \"http_status\": 200, \"fetched_at\": \"2026-11-05...\", \"length\": <len>, \"fetch_sha256\": <sha256 of body>, \"quote\": \"<the located quote>\", \"span\": {\"start\": <int>, \"end\": <int>}} — span indexes into the saved body text such that body_text[start:end] equals the quote (whitespace-normalised comparison is used by the tool, but byte the span to the exact substring). Save the raw body at quote-receipts/raw/S496.body.\n   Self-check BEFORE yield: `python3 -B corpus/audit_source_quotes.py verify --sources <a copy of corpus/SOURCES.md with your S496 row appended> --receipts /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-93/w1/ScoutRecord/quote-receipts --sid S496` must print `S496 terminal=S496 state=verified` and `SUMMARY ... unresolved=0` (exit 0). Run the check on a COPY of SOURCES.md in your scratch, never on the lane file.\n5. Write /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-93/w1/ScoutRecord/sources-draft.md: both row texts + the located quotes + access dates. Write it EARLY (first 15 minutes) so the scribe can wait for it.\n6. Write /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-93/w1/ScoutRecord/opens.json: {\"record_sha256\": \"b045a4eecf2d77cfdee5de83e5864fcadbd6fd54e749f6985a04ecbeebaae868\", \"oracle_tail\": \"ORACLE OK (17/17 checks)\", \"fixture_shas\": {\"index.html\": \"46e51761af28b05c4c382c8ee72f9d77fee6f20d0b904f69b1c7f9a2214deb45\", \"app.js\": \"fb079fa20d08a1309bed44c80743293d37ec8cd51c7ef7f9ee465e0d0d5aa593\"}}.\n\n# Acceptance\noracle.log ends with the 17/17 line; digests.txt shows the three pinned hashes; opens.json matches the pins exactly; S496 verifies through the audit tool on your scratch copy; sources-draft.md exists with both rows; nothing outside your wave dir was written.\n\nReport: .ufo/waves/round-93/w1/ScoutRecord.md\n\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch.\nJudged on: coverage\nMilestone: Round 93: C1 K 9/15->10/15 (C08 entry from the saved r77 CDP record, provenance gate); C2 successor counters kill 9 routed forgery classes; 13 seats\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-93/w1/ScoutRecord.md"
