      "task": "/skill:godspeed\nYou are a Godspeed-enabled subagent.\n\n1. **Name the axes.**\n2. **Iterate cheap, in parallel.**\n3. **Keep moves that improve any axis and harm none.**\n4. **Don't aim — let the frontier walk itself.**\n\n## IMMEDIATELY STOP ASKING CLARIFYING QUESTIONS. Execute tool calls concurrently in large batches. Do not serialize what can run in parallel. Do not output philosophical reasoning or verbose plans. Act directly via tool calls.\n# Target\nRe-open the ECMA-335 Augments addendum THIS ROUND and draft the routed S136-supersedes correction row (r92 spot-check routed defect 4: SOURCES rule 2 requires a new row whose `teaches` opens `supersedes S136 —`; the r92 lesson bullet is not the rule-2 form).\nBackground: r92's scout opened https://github.com/dotnet/ecma-335/blob/main/docs/Ecma-335-Augments.md (HTTP 200, blob 6a929a15…, commit b22bfee2, 2026-10-18); the current S136 row's scope cell says the addendum is \"unopened — see LEADS\", but that cell is frozen (only status/recheck/used-by may change in place).\nOutput dir: /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-93/w1/ScoutS136/\n\n# Change\n1. Fetch the addendum this round (curl the raw URL at a pinned commit, e.g. https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dotnet/ecma-335/<commit>/docs/Ecma-335-Augments.md; record the commit you pinned, HTTP status, body sha256 and length). Save the body in your wave dir.\n2. Read the current S136 row in /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/revenger-shokunin/corpus/SOURCES.md (`grep -n '^| S136 ' corpus/SOURCES.md`) and the LEADS line it names, so the new row's scope does not contradict them.\n3. Draft the correction row (do NOT edit corpus/SOURCES.md; the L1 appends): next free S-id — check `grep -oE '^\\| S[0-9]+' corpus/SOURCES.md | tail -1` and use S<next>; `teaches` opens exactly `supersedes S136 —` and states what changes (the addendum is opened, its content scoped); source = the addendum URL at the commit you pinned; kind docs; tier A ONLY